<title>USA: Tracor unit gets McDonnell Douglas contract.</title>
<headline>Tracor unit gets McDonnell Douglas contract.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tracor Inc said on Wednesday its Tracor Flight Systems Inc subsidiary  won a $27 million contract from McDonnell Douglas Corp to make the y-barrel assembly for the MD-95 twin jet.</p>
<p>Tracor last year signed a $30 million contract with McDonnell Douglas to join the wing halves for the twin jet.</p>
<p>The y-barrel assemblies will be manufactured in Palmdale, Calif., creating more than 100 jobs there. The contract is for 10 years.</p>
</text>
